1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Returning to a project can be difficult.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,500
The files are still there,
but the context is lost.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:16,000
We may forget what changed,
why a decision was made, and what to do next.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
This is Nexus Atlas.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It helps people keep the context
of long-term work.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It connects project history, knowledge,
decisions, actions, and trusted data.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Nexus does not start
with an empty chat.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
It starts with Atlas Desk.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Here, Nexus finds Verity,
a project inactive for twenty-one days.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The project now needs re-entry.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Atlas Map shows the most important path
for the current task.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
For Verity, it connects the evaluation rules,
Benchmark v1, calibration, results, and release evidence.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,500
It only shows the context
that matters now.

14
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:23,000
Nexus restores four important changes
and four valid decisions.

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,500
It also finds two old evidence records,
one agent conflict, and one missing owner.

16
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:39,000
Nexus shows what can still be trusted,
and what must be checked or repaired.

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
One agent recommends more features.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Another recommends better evaluation quality.

19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Nexus keeps both suggestions.

20
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
The user confirms
the Benchmark-first direction.

21
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,500
DataHub shows that Benchmark v1
has no owner.

22
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:13,500
Nexus shows the exact asset,
the current value, and the proposed owner.

23
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:21,500
After the user confirms,
Nexus updates DataHub and reads it again.

24
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:28,500
The issue is closed only after
the new owner is verified.

25
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:32,000
The project can now continue.

26
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:41,000
The next steps are to build the test set,
run older samples, and adjust the scoring rules.

27
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Nexus turns project history into a clear path
from context, to decision, to action, and memory.
